{"question": "According to Chapter II, who should take over the planning that workers previously did themselves, and what should that planning be based on?", "retrieval_history": [{"tool": "search", "queries": ["Chapter II planning workers"], "context": "[1a4f686bab0b85066fa7e5fc1b6a899858ef9a7c0eaa6bb523b74d18d39a32bc | data/raw/project_gutenberg/pg6435/pg6435-images.html | page 43]
Doubtless some of those who are especially interested in working men will complain because under scientific management the workman, when he is shown how to do twice as much work as he formerly did, is not paid twice his former wages, while others who are more interested in the dividends than the workmen will complain that under this system the men receive much higher wages than they did before.

It does seem grossly unjust when the bare statement is made that the competent pig-iron handler, for instance, who has been so trained that he piles 3 6/10 times as much iron as the incompetent man formerly did, should receive an increase of only 60 per cent in wages.", "context_ids": ["1a4f686bab0b85066fa7e5fc1b6a899858ef9a7c0eaa6bb523b74d18d39a32bc"]}], "output_schema": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"action": {"type": "string", "enum": ["search", "answer", "abstain"]}, "query": {"type": "string"}, "answer": {"type": "string"}, "citations": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "reason": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["action", "query", "answer", "citations", "reason"]}}

{"question": "In Taylor's description of task management, how much is added to ordinary wages, and what conditions must a worker meet to receive it?", "retrieval_history": [{"tool": "search", "queries": ["Taylor task management ordinary wages"], "context": "[a9c1ebd5debf1e2ed6d40ebaced1f0aec902900f8f962d5bd5919bcb6a34cf79 | data/raw/project_gutenberg/pg6435/pg6435-images.html | page 9]
THE FINEST TYPE OF ORDINARY MANAGEMENT

Before starting to illustrate the principles of scientific management, or "task management" as it is briefly called, it seems desirable to outline what the writer believes will be recognized as the best type of management which is in common use. This is done so that the great difference between the best of the ordinary management and scientific management may be fully appreciated.", "context_ids": ["a9c1ebd5debf1e2ed6d40ebaced1f0aec902900f8f962d5bd5919bcb6a34cf79"]}], "output_schema": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"action": {"type": "string", "enum": ["search", "answer", "abstain"]}, "query": {"type": "string"}, "answer": {"type": "string"}, "citations": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "reason": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["action", "query", "answer", "citations", "reason"]}}

